## 2. 3D Modeling Playground & Tile Geometry Engine (Non-Commercial & Evaluation License)

All source code, geometric algorithms, parametric folding logic, state machines, node graph calculations, and GLTF parsing logic relating to the **3D Modeling Playground** (including but not limited to files located in `src/components/scene/`, `src/components/playCanvas.tsx`, `src/components/Rig.tsx`, `src/components/tex-tile.tsx`, `src/components/fold-control.tsx`, `src/components/base-control.tsx`, `src/components/ghost-arrow.tsx`, `src/components/spinFlatform.tsx`, `src/hooks/use-play-canvas.ts`, `src/types/tile.ts`, `parse_glb.js`, and `parse_glb_bbox.js`) are subject to the following terms:

### A. Permitted Uses
- **Personal & Academic Evaluation**: You may view, clone, run, and modify the 3D Playground code locally solely for non-commercial personal experimentation, educational study, academic research, and portfolio evaluation.
- **Contributions**: You may submit pull requests, bug fixes, or performance improvements to this repository for consideration by the Unstitch maintainers.

### B. Prohibited Uses
- **No Commercial Exploitation**: You may NOT use, distribute, sublicense, host, embed, or deploy the 3D Playground code, geometry engine, or folding algorithms in any commercial software, SaaS product, client project, paid service, or revenue-generating platform without prior written authorization from Unstitch.
- **No Derivative Commercial Engines**: You may NOT extract, reverse-engineer, or adapt the interlocking textile geometry calculations or folding state engine to create competing 3D modeling tools or textile simulation software.
- **No Unauthorized Physical Production**: You may NOT utilize the parametric algorithms or geometry outputs to mass-produce or sell commercial physical interlocking modular textile goods without a commercial license.

